# Imodane, the Pyrohammer: the spell that deals the damage is the one the ability asks about, not another spell beneath it. Bot1 casts
# Lightning Bolt at Bot2's face, then in response Lightning Bolt at Bot2's Ornithopter. The second resolves first: it targets only a
# single creature, so Imodane's trigger (3 to Bot2) goes above the first Bolt (3 to Bot2), 20 -> 17 -> 14. The Bolt beneath, aimed at
# a player, would not have triggered anything if it were the one asked about.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Imodane, the Pyrohammer
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Imodane, the Pyrohammer.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 2
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter = (absent)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 14
